# Bourgatov

id:world-bourgatov a oa:Place, oa:World ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bourgatov" ;
    oa:article <https://www.orionsarm.com/eg-article/46100f97c38ac> ;
    oa:kind "planet" ;
    oa:labelsSystem false ;
    oa:note "Theta Persei, 36.6 ly. \"Thinly populated by Radiation Nation tweaks, various scavengers and archaeologists\" today, no polity of this file. Refugees went on to the asteroid belt at Iota Persei, \"the last (known) inhabitants\" of which \"left in 9300\", and to New Magnitogorsk in the Middle Regions; neither is placed on this map. The clan's original home, the asteroid Bourgatow, was towed here in the 3700's AT and later vanished to \"a secret location\", per its own page, \"a hidden treasure trove somewhere in interstellar space\" in popular myth since." ;
    oa:systemName "Bourgatov" ;
    oa:uncertain false .

claim:location-world-bourgatov a prov:Entity, oa:LocationClaim ;
    prov:hadPrimarySource <https://www.orionsarm.com/eg-article/46100f97c38ac> ;
    oa:about id:world-bourgatov ;
    oa:canonical true ;
    oa:catalogueFromSource false ;
    oa:knownDistanceConflict false ;
    oa:method oa:DirectTranscription ;
    oa:starName "Theta Persei" .

claim:event-world-bourgatov-001 a prov:Entity, oa:EventClaim ;
    oa:about id:world-bourgatov ;
    oa:canonical true ;
    oa:eventKind oa:Settled ;
    oa:note "The Bourgatov Alliance's own page, as pasted by the project owner: \"During the 2000's AT the terraforming investments began to truly pay off, and the Bourgatow used their vast wealth to relocate their headquarters to the newly terraformed Theta Persei III, which they renamed Bourgatov.\" Capital from the same move, per the Corona article: \"Bourgatov, the capital of the Bourgatov Alliance\", undated there. \"Politically Bourgatov, still owned and run by the Bourgatov clan transaps, carefully weathered all political upheavals\" through the First and Second Consolidation Wars and into the Integration, \"a major power ... with a total wealth nearly equal to the major empires\", down to the Version War's outbreak at Bourgatov in 4476 and the collapse of 4490 below. The clan itself goes back much further, to the asteroid Bourgatow in the Old Solar System, settled in the 390's AT; not placed on this map, and kept as context in the note below." ;
    oa:polity id:polity-bourgatov-alliance ;
    oa:precision oa:Between ;
    oa:recordOrder 0 ;
    oa:sourceDescription "sources/polities/bourgatov-alliance.txt" ;
    oa:untilAT 2099 ;
    oa:yearAT 2000 .

claim:event-world-bourgatov-002 a prov:Entity, oa:EventClaim ;
    oa:about id:world-bourgatov ;
    oa:canonical true ;
    oa:eventKind oa:Abandoned ;
    oa:note "\"As the advanced infrastructure broke down in the assaults of AI viruses, nanoswarms and economic chaos ... the biospheres were infiltrated with nanoweapons, forcing people into space ... By 4490 AT the initial population of 34 billion had been reduced to a mere 490 million.\" The shorter world-profile article (eg-article/46100f97c38ac) gives the same figures by way of an unnamed faction's runaway \"hunter-seeker virus\" blight rather than the Version War's proxy conflict named here; likely the same event through two tellings, not a real contradiction. \"The other Bourgatov Alliance worlds fared better, but were all absorbed by various empires. Of the Bourgatov clan, only a handful of relativistic journeyers survived. They later congregated on Corona during the ComEmp period where they remain in cryonic suspension to this day\" -- none of this is placed on the map." ;
    oa:precision oa:NotLaterThan ;
    oa:recordOrder 1 ;
    oa:sourceDescription "sources/polities/bourgatov-alliance.txt" ;
    oa:yearAT 4490 .

